# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Appendix: Krylov subspace from real time-evolutions {#appendix-krylov-"
"subspace-from-real-time-evolutions}"
msgstr ""
"Apéndice: Subespacio de Krylov a partir de evoluciones temporales reales "
"{#appendix-krylov-subspace-from-real-time-evolutions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The unitary Krylov space is defined as\n"
msgstr "El espacio de Krylov unitario se define como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ |\\psi\\rangle,  e^{-iH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-irH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ |\\psi\\rangle,  e^{-iH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-irH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some timestep $dt$ that we will determine later. Temporarily assume $r$ "
"is even: then define $d=r/2$. Notice that when we project the Hamiltonian "
"into the Krylov space above, it is indistinguishable from the Krylov space\n"
msgstr ""
"para algún paso temporal $dt$ que determinaremos más adelante. Supón "
"temporalmente que $r$ es par: entonces define $d=r/2$. Observa que cuando "
"proyectamos el Hamiltoniano en el espacio de Krylov anterior, es "
"indistinguible del espacio de Krylov\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ e^{i\\,d\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle,  e^{i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, e^{-i\\,d\\,H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ e^{i\\,d\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle,  e^{i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, e^{-i\\,d\\,H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that is, where all the time-evolutions are shifted backward by $d$ timesteps.\n"
"The reason it is indistinguishable is because the matrix elements\n"
msgstr ""
"es decir, donde todas las evoluciones temporales se desplazan hacia atrás $d$ pasos temporales.\n"
"La razón por la que es indistinguible es porque los elementos de la matriz\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{j,k} = \\langle\\psi|e^{i\\,j\\,H\\,dt}He^{-i\\,k\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle=\\langle\\psi|He^{i(j-k)H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{j,k} = \\langle\\psi|e^{i\\,j\\,H\\,dt}He^{-i\\,k\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle=\\langle\\psi|He^{i(j-k)H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"are invariant under overall shifts of the evolution time, since the time-"
"evolutions commute with the Hamiltonian. For odd $r$, we can use the "
"analysis for $r-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"son invariantes bajo desplazamientos globales del tiempo de evolución, ya "
"que las evoluciones temporales conmutan con el Hamiltoniano. Para $r$ impar,"
" podemos usar el análisis para $r-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to show that somewhere in this Krylov space, there is guaranteed to "
"be a low-energy state. We do so by way of the following result, which is "
"derived from Theorem 3.1 in [\\[3\\]](#references):\n"
msgstr ""
"Queremos demostrar que en algún lugar de este espacio de Krylov existe "
"garantizadamente un estado de baja energía. Lo hacemos mediante el siguiente"
" resultado, que se deriva del Teorema 3.1 en [\\[3\\]](#references):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Claim 1:** there exists a function $f$ such that for energies $E$ in the spectral range of the Hamiltonian (that is, between the ground state energy and the maximum energy)...\n"
"1. $f(E_0)=1$\n"
"2. $|f(E)|\\le2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d}$ for all values of $E$ that lie $\\ge\\delta$ away from $E_0$, that is, it is exponentially suppressed\n"
"3. $f(E)$ is a linear combination of $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ for $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Afirmación 1:** existe una función $f$ tal que para energías $E$ en el rango espectral del Hamiltoniano (es decir, entre la energía del estado fundamental y la energía máxima)...\n"
"1. $f(E_0)=1$\n"
"2. $|f(E)|\\le2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d}$ para todos los valores de $E$ que se encuentran a una distancia $\\ge\\delta$ de $E_0$, es decir, está exponencialmente suprimida\n"
"3. $f(E)$ es una combinación lineal de $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ para $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We give a proof below, but that can be safely skipped unless one wants to "
"understand the full, rigorous argument. For now we focus on the implications"
" of the above claim. By property 3 above, we can see that the shifted Krylov"
" space above contains the state $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$. This is our low-energy"
" state. To see why, write $|\\psi\\rangle$ in the energy eigenbasis:\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación proporcionamos una demostración, pero puede omitirse sin "
"problema a menos que se desee comprender el argumento riguroso completo. Por"
" ahora nos centramos en las implicaciones de la afirmación anterior. Por la "
"propiedad 3 anterior, podemos ver que el espacio de Krylov desplazado "
"contiene el estado $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$. Este es nuestro estado de baja "
"energía. Para ver por qué, escribe $|\\psi\\rangle$ en la base de "
"eigenenergías:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_k|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_k|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $|E_k\\rangle$ is the kth energy eigenstate and $\\gamma_k$ is its "
"amplitude in the initial state $|\\psi\\rangle$. Expressed in terms of this,"
" $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$ is given by\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $|E_k\\rangle$ es el k-ésimo estado propio de energía y $\\gamma_k$ es"
" su amplitud en el estado inicial $|\\psi\\rangle$. Expresado en estos "
"términos, $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$ viene dado por\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f(H)|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_kf(E_k)|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f(H)|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_kf(E_k)|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"using the fact that we can replace $H$ by $E_k$ when it acts on the "
"eigenstate $|E_k\\rangle$. The energy error of this state is therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"usando el hecho de que podemos reemplazar $H$ por $E_k$ cuando actúa sobre "
"el estado propio $|E_k\\rangle$. El error de energía de este estado es por "
"lo tanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\langle\\psi|f(H)(H-E_0)f(H)|\\psi\\rangle}{\\langle\\psi|f(H)^2|\\psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\langle\\psi|f(H)(H-E_0)f(H)|\\psi\\rangle}{\\langle\\psi|f(H)^2|\\psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"= \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"= \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To turn this into an upper bound that is easier to understand, we first "
"separate the sum in the numerator into terms with $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ and "
"terms with $E_k-E_0>\\delta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para convertir esto en una cota superior más fácil de entender, primero "
"separamos la suma en el numerador en términos con $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ y "
"términos con $E_k-E_0>\\delta$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} + \\frac{\\sum_{E_k> E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} + \\frac{\\sum_{E_k> E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can upper bound the first term by $\\delta$,\n"
msgstr "Podemos acotar superiormente el primer término por $\\delta$,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} < \\frac{\\delta\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} \\le \\delta,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} < \\frac{\\delta\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} \\le \\delta,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first step follows because $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ for every $E_k$ in"
" the sum, and the second step follows because the sum in the numerator is a "
"subset of the sum in the denominator. For the second term, first we lower "
"bound the denominator by $|\\gamma_0|^2$, since $f(E_0)^2=1$: adding "
"everything back together, this gives\n"
msgstr ""
"donde el primer paso se sigue porque $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ para cada $E_k$ en"
" la suma, y el segundo paso se sigue porque la suma en el numerador es un "
"subconjunto de la suma en el denominador. Para el segundo término, primero "
"acotamos inferiormente el denominador por $|\\gamma_0|^2$, dado que "
"$f(E_0)^2=1$: sumando todo nuevamente, esto da\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{1}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{1}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simplify what is left, notice that for all these $E_k$, by the definition"
" of $f$ we know that $f(E_k)^2 \\le 4\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}$. "
"Additionally upper bounding $E_k-E_0<2\\|H\\|$ and upper bounding "
"$\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2<1$ gives\n"
msgstr ""
"Para simplificar lo que queda, observa que para todos estos $E_k$, por la "
"definición de $f$ sabemos que $f(E_k)^2 \\le 4\\left(1 + "
"\\delta\\right)^{-2d}$. Adicionalmente, acotando superiormente $E_k-"
"E_0<2\\|H\\|$ y acotando superiormente "
"$\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2<1$ obtenemos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{8}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\|H\\|\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{8}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\|H\\|\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This holds for any $\\delta>0$, so if we set $\\delta$ equal to our goal "
"error, then the error bound above converges towards that exponentially with "
"the Krylov dimension $2d=r$. Also note that if $\\delta<E_1-E_0$ then the "
"$\\delta$ term actually goes away entirely in the above bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto es válido para cualquier $\\delta>0$, por lo que si establecemos "
"$\\delta$ igual a nuestro error objetivo, entonces la cota de error anterior"
" converge hacia ese valor exponencialmente con la dimensión de Krylov "
"$2d=r$. También note que si $\\delta<E_1-E_0$ entonces el término $\\delta$ "
"en realidad desaparece por completo en la cota anterior.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To complete the argument, we first note that the above is just the energy "
"error of the particular state $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$, rather than the energy "
"error of the lowest energy state in the Krylov space. However, by the "
"(Rayleigh-Ritz) variational principle, the energy error of the lowest energy"
" state in the Krylov space is upper bounded by the energy error of any state"
" in the Krylov space, so the above is also an upper bound on the energy "
"error of the lowest energy state, that is, the output of the Krylov quantum "
"diagonalization algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para completar el argumento, primero notamos que lo anterior es solo el "
"error de energía del estado particular $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$, en lugar del "
"error de energía del estado de menor energía en el espacio de Krylov. Sin "
"embargo, por el principio variacional (de Rayleigh-Ritz), el error de "
"energía del estado de menor energía en el espacio de Krylov está acotado "
"superiormente por el error de energía de cualquier estado en el espacio de "
"Krylov, por lo que lo anterior también es una cota superior del error de "
"energía del estado de menor energía, es decir, la salida del algoritmo de "
"diagonalización cuántica de Krylov.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A similar analysis as the above can be carried out that additionally "
"accounts for noise and the thresholding procedure discussed in the notebook."
" See [\\[2\\]](#references) and [\\[4\\]](#references) for this analysis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Se puede realizar un análisis similar al anterior que además tenga en cuenta"
" el ruido y el procedimiento de umbralización discutido en el cuaderno. "
"Consulta [\\[2\\]](#references) y [\\[4\\]](#references) para este "
"análisis.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix: proof of Claim 1 {#appendix-proof-of-claim-1}"
msgstr ""
"Apéndice: demostración de la Afirmación 1 {#appendix-proof-of-claim-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following is mostly derived from [\\[3\\]](#references), Theorem 3.1: "
"let $ 0 < a < b $ and let $ \\Pi^*_d $ be the space of residual polynomials "
"(polynomials whose value at 0 is 1) of degree at most $ d $. The solution "
"to\n"
msgstr ""
"Lo siguiente se deriva principalmente de [\\[3\\]](#references), Teorema "
"3.1: sean $ 0 < a < b $ y sea $ \\Pi^*_d $ el espacio de polinomios "
"residuales (polinomios cuyo valor en 0 es 1) de grado a lo sumo $ d $. La "
"solución de\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = \\min_{p \\in \\Pi^*_d} \\max_{x \\in [a, b]} |p(x)| \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = \\min_{p \\in \\Pi^*_d} \\max_{x \\in [a, b]} |p(x)| \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is\n"
msgstr "es\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p^*(x) = \\frac{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a - 2x}{b - a}\\right)}{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right)}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p^*(x) = \\frac{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a - 2x}{b - a}\\right)}{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right)}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the corresponding minimal value is\n"
msgstr "y el valor mínimo correspondiente es\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to convert this into a function that can be expressed naturally in terms of complex exponentials, because those are the real time-evolutions that generate the quantum Krylov space.\n"
"To do so, it is convenient to introduce the following transformation of energies within the spectral range of the Hamiltonian to numbers in the range $[0,1]$: define\n"
msgstr ""
"Queremos convertir esto en una función que pueda expresarse naturalmente en términos de exponenciales complejas, porque estas son las evoluciones temporales reales que generan el espacio cuántico de Krylov.\n"
"Para ello, es conveniente introducir la siguiente transformación de energías dentro del rango espectral del Hamiltoniano a números en el rango $[0,1]$: defina\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"g(E) = \\frac{1-\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big)}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"g(E) = \\frac{1-\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big)}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $dt$ is a timestep such that $-\\pi < E_0dt < E_\\text{max}dt < \\pi$.\n"
"Notice that $g(E_0)=0$ and $g(E)$ grows as $E$ moves away from $E_0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $dt$ es un paso temporal tal que $-\\pi < E_0dt < E_\\text{max}dt < \\pi$.\n"
"Observa que $g(E_0)=0$ y $g(E)$ crece a medida que $E$ se aleja de $E_0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now using the polynomial $p^*(x)$ with the parameters a, b, d set to $a = "
"g(E_0 + \\delta)$, $b = 1$, and d = int(r/2), we define the function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora, usando el polinomio $p^*(x)$ con los parámetros a, b, d establecidos "
"como $a = g(E_0 + \\delta)$, $b = 1$, y d = int(r/2), definimos la "
"función:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f(E) = p^* \\left( g(E) \\right) = \\frac{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big) - \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 +\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f(E) = p^* \\left( g(E) \\right) = \\frac{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big) - \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 +\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $E_0$ is the ground state energy. We can see by inserting "
"$\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}$ that $f(E)$ is a trigonometric "
"polynomial of degree $d$, that is, a linear combination of $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ "
"for $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$. Furthermore, from the definition of $p^*(x)$ "
"above we have that $f(E_0)=p(0)=1$ and for any $E$ in the spectral range "
"such that $\\vert E-E_0 \\vert > \\delta$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $E_0$ es la energía del estado fundamental. Podemos ver al insertar "
"$\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}$ que $f(E)$ es un polinomio "
"trigonométrico de grado $d$, es decir, una combinación lineal de "
"$e^{ijE\\,dt}$ para $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$. Además, de la definición de "
"$p^*(x)$ anterior tenemos que $f(E_0)=p(0)=1$ y para cualquier $E$ en el "
"rango espectral tal que $\\vert E-E_0 \\vert > \\delta$ tenemos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|f(E)| \\le \\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|f(E)| \\le \\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\leq 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d} = 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-\\lfloor k/2\\rfloor}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\leq 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d} = 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-\\lfloor k/2\\rfloor}.\n"
"$$\n"

